#Data: hprice1 (price = house price in thousands of dollars; bdrms = number of bedrooms; sqrft = size of the house in square feet). The simple regression of price on bdrms leaves out sqrft. Run the multiple regression lm(price ~ bdrms + sqrft, data = hprice1) and the regression of the omitted variable on the included one, lm(sqrft ~ bdrms, data = hprice1). Compute β̂2·δ̃1: the sqrft coefficient from the multiple regression times the bdrms slope from the second regression.
data(hprice1)
MLR = lm(price ~ bdrms + sqrft, data = hprice1)
SLR = lm(sqrft ~ bdrms, data = hprice1)

MLR$coefficients["sqrft"] * SLR$coefficients["bdrms"] 
